  <constraints>
    <constraint source="INCOMING §5 Item 2 (BINDING)">
      Introduce ONE shared `TenancyModel` enum. Adopt PARSE-OR-REJECT, not defaulting. Parse at the edge, pass
      a typed value inward. All four silent-default sites (H2a:284, H2b:289, AiSearchTenantFilterInvariantProbe:240,
      ArmCostEnvelopeChecker:268) disappear — they are NOT individually corrected. H1 already implements the
      target behaviour and provides the pattern; the enum generalises it.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="INCOMING §5 Item 2 P-2 defect (BINDING)">
      `H1SubscriptionReadinessHandler.CustomerOwnedTenancyValues = { "CustomerOwned", "Model2Dedicated" }` maps
      the single literal `Model2Dedicated` to `CustomerOwned` unconditionally, so H1 demands Lighthouse
      delegation for subscriptions Spaarke already owns. The *ownership* vocabulary (`SpaarkeOwned` /
      `CustomerOwned`) is already correct and D-12's model axis maps onto it: Model 1 → SpaarkeOwned, Model 2
      → CustomerOwned. Retire the two *model* literals from these sets. Do NOT redesign the classifier.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="D-12-code-branch-inventory.md §4 (BINDING sequencing)">
      The enum MUST carry the rejection behaviour, NOT the defaulting behaviour. `Model1SharedFloorEnvelopeUsd`
      (ArmCostEnvelopeChecker option) becomes meaningless when the shared tier retires — DELETE the option +
      its config binding + its `_` arm; the honest default is *no default* (rejection, matching H1). Do NOT
      relabel `sprk_tenancymodel` (Item 3's job — value 1 fans by Profile). Item 2 does NOT precipitate that.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="INCOMING §5 Item 2 test-rewrite obligation (BINDING)">
      `AiSearchTenantFilterInvariantProbeTests.ProbeAsync_Model2_UnspecifiedTenancyModel_DefaultsToModel2_ReturnsPassed`
      pins the defaulting as a contract. **Rewrite it, don't mechanically update it** — the test's PURPOSE flips
      from "verify D3 defaulting" to "verify D3 rejection". New test name should reflect the new intent (e.g.,
      `ProbeAsync_UnspecifiedTenancyModel_Rejects_WithNoDefault`).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="H12c idempotency-key format preservation (BINDING)">
      `H12cRuntimeReferencesHandler` builds idempotency keys as `h12c-{customerId}-{tenancyModel}-{hash}` (or
      similar — verify at execution time via grep). The tenancy string embedded here MUST remain
      `"Model1Shared"` / `"Model2Dedicated"` EXACTLY, byte-for-byte. Enum names + `.ToString()` output +
      JSON serialization all preserve these string values. Any completed H12c phase whose key was built with
      the pre-Item-2 format MUST replay as a durable no-op on Item-2 post-deployment. Item 3 owns any actual
      string-value change; Item 2 does NOT change strings.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="Cosmos wire-format preservation (BINDING)">
      `ProvisioningRun.TenancyModel` stays a `string` field for Cosmos-on-disk stability. The enum is a
      COMPUTED helper (`ProvisioningRun.ParsedTenancyModel { get; }` or equivalent), NOT a replacement
      property. Existing rows in Cosmos MUST deserialize identically post-Item-2; changing the field type or
      adding a `[JsonConverter]` risks breaking existing state. Handlers call `TenancyModelParser.TryParse` at
      entry — same pattern H1 already uses today (`InvalidTenancyModel` rejection code).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §6.5 (ADR Conflict Resolution Protocol)">
      Path C (pivot to comply) applies — code moves to comply with D-12. No Path A/B expected unless a
      cross-project consumer of `H1SubscriptionReadinessHandler.CustomerOwnedTenancyValues` public surface
      surfaces (unlikely; internal helper). Silent violation FORBIDDEN — escalate any unexpected caller
      surface change per §6.5 Path A/B/C framing.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §8 test-modifying override">
      Task modifies `*Tests/**` — UNCONDITIONAL FULL rigor + UNCONDITIONAL Step 9.5 quality gates
      (code-review + adr-check).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7 KEEP-path forcing-function discipline">
      Test deletions/rewrites are permitted ONLY when the code path being tested is retired (the D3 defaulting
      test) or when the test-fixture data must be mechanically updated (the ~25 fixture sites setting
      `TenancyModel = "..."`). New tests SHOULD be authored where the enum + parser introduce new behaviour
      (`TenancyModelParser.TryParse` deserves round-trip + reject-on-blank + reject-on-unknown + case-sensitivity
      tests). Do NOT scope-narrow or `[Skip]` any existing test. ArchTest suite MUST remain 326/326.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4 (posture preservation)">
      Item 2 introduces NO new `.WithClientSecret(...)` sites, NO new `ClientSecretCredential(...)`
      constructions. The enum + parser touch tenancy routing, not credential construction. The narrow r1 Path A
      exception at ADR-028 concise L220 (WorkerDataverseCredentialFactory prong-3 for spaarkedev1) is UNTOUCHED.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>
      If preflight grep reveals a consumer of the string literals `"Model1Shared"` / `"Model2Dedicated"` or the
      set fields `CustomerOwnedTenancyValues` / `SpaarkeOwnedTenancyValues` OUTSIDE the enumerated in-scope
      files (see the IMPLICIT scope note below) — STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6. Likely candidates:
      (a) a parallel worktree added a new consumer since master merge; (b) `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml`
      or `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml` references the literals (Section 6 sweep territory — but a
      code-side consumer in `src/` would be a scope-widening); (c) an integration test outside
      `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests`. Do NOT silently expand scope.
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If H12c's idempotency-key building code embeds the tenancy string in a format other than the expected
      literal — STOP + investigate. The BINDING preservation constraint requires the key format to remain
      byte-for-byte identical. If the format includes a lowercase transform / hash-only / etc. that already
      "normalizes" away the literal, verify with the H12c owner (task-execute Step 6 → owner escalation) BEFORE
      changing anything.
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If `dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/` drops below 326/326 post-change — STOP. The enum + parser
      migration should NEVER regress an ArchTest. Debug the specific ArchTest; do NOT bulk-modify. If the
      violation is a genuine ArchTest semantic conflict with the enum design, it's a §6.5 Path A/B/C decision.
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` shows more than 23 baseline
      failures (task 221 domain: 17× FileKvSecretManifestTests + 6× CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests) —
      STOP + stash-and-compare to isolate whether the new failure is Item 2-caused or a downstream shift from
      the recent master-merge landscape.
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If a hit surfaces in ANY of these HOT locations, STOP and escalate — these indicate scope-crossing into
      another owner's blast radius: (a) `.github/workflows/**` (build pipeline references); (b)
      `infrastructure/bicep/**` (Bicep parameter references — Item 4's territory); (c)
      `.claude/skills/provision-environment/**` (L3 operator skill contract); (d) any file under
      `projects/unified-access-control-r2/**` or `projects/auth-v*/**` (parallel-worktree hot-path per
      projects/INDEX.md).
    </trigger>
    <trigger>
      If executing step 5b (H1 P-2 defect closure) reveals the `CustomerOwnedTenancyValues` /
      `SpaarkeOwnedTenancyValues` sets are consumed OUTSIDE the H1 handler (public / cross-handler surface) —
      STOP + escalate. The inventory §3 characterizes these as H1-private; a public consumer would require a
      §6.5 Path A/B/C decision on the ownership vocabulary.
    </trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>H1SubscriptionReadinessHandler already implements the target parse-or-reject pattern (`InvalidTenancyModel` rejection code). H3EntraAppRegHandler.IsRecognizedTenancyModel is a smaller instance of the same pattern. The enum + parser GENERALISE this existing pattern; they do not invent a new one.</existing>
    <extension>N/A — the enum is genuinely NEW surface. Extension is not possible: no existing type carries the two tenancy values as a discriminated set. The parser (`TenancyModelParser.TryParse`) mirrors `Enum.TryParse&lt;T&gt;` but adds the case-sensitivity + null-handling contract H1 already implements ad hoc.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every future tenancy-conditional handler re-derives the string-comparison + defaulting decision independently. Four sites already disagree (D1/D2/D3 default to Model 2; D4 defaults to the retired shared tier). B8 rejects wrong-case where B1–B7 accept it. The P-2 defect demands Lighthouse delegation for Spaarke-owned subscriptions RIGHT NOW. Every one of these is a live bug D-12's remediation is designed to close atomically; deferring locks in the divergence.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step n="0" name="Preflight — verify 326/326 baseline + grep the full consumer surface">
      Run BEFORE touching any file:
      1. `dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/Spaarke.ArchTests.csproj --no-build` — must be 326/326 (task-222
         baseline). If fewer, STOP + reconcile before starting.
      2. Full grep sweep (capture output as scratch file):
         `git grep -n "Model1Shared\|Model2Dedicated\|CustomerOwnedTenancyValues\|SpaarkeOwnedTenancyValues\|Model1TenancyModel\|Model2TenancyModel\|Model1SharedFloorEnvelopeUsd\|Model1MarginalEnvelopeUsd\|Model2EmptyEnvelopeUsd" -- 'src/**/*.cs'`
      3. Categorize each hit:
         - **Production branch site** — routes control flow → migrate to enum switch (in-scope)
         - **Production silent default** — coerces blank/unknown → replace with reject (in-scope)
         - **Production const / options field** — being retired (in-scope)
         - **Production XML doc / comment** — inventory §5 AP-12 surface (in-scope, mechanical)
         - **Test fixture (`= "Model1Shared"`)** — mechanical enum update (in-scope; ~25 sites per inventory)
         - **Test method name / assertion using literal** — mechanical enum reference update (in-scope)
         - **File OUTSIDE `src/` or `tests/`** — potential scope-widening; escalate per trigger 1
      4. Verify no uncommitted work: `git status` — must be clean (task 222's commit landed 1e586978f).
      5. Verify H12c idempotency-key format: grep for H12c key construction pattern to confirm the tenancy
         literal is embedded as-is (not hashed / lowercased / normalized). If NOT the expected format →
         escalation trigger 2.
    </step>

    <step n="1" name="Create the shared TenancyModel enum + TenancyModelParser">
      Create `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Models/TenancyModel.cs`:
      1. `public enum TenancyModel { Model1Shared = 0, Model2Dedicated = 1 }` — explicit integer values match
         current `sprk_tenancymodel` option-set integers per `Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1:211,217-218`
         (Model1Shared = 0, Model2Dedicated = 1 — verify current script if inventory outdated). Reserved
         numeric ordering enables future Item 3 fan-by-Profile without renumbering.
      2. `public static class TenancyModelParser`:
         - `public static bool TryParse(string? value, out TenancyModel model)` — returns true only for exact
           case-sensitive match `"Model1Shared"` or `"Model2Dedicated"`. Null / whitespace / any other value
           returns false. Case-sensitivity matches H1 + H3 (the two fail-loud sites); ArmCostEnvelopeChecker's
           B8 was case-sensitive by accident but happens to align. The rewrite forces this alignment
           intentionally.
         - `public static TenancyModel Parse(string? value)` — throws `TenancyModelParseException` on failure
           (a new sealed exception in the same file). Reserved for callers that KNOW the value has been
           pre-validated (Handlers that already ran a `TryParse` earlier in the request lifecycle).
         - No `ParseOrDefault` overload. No `ParseIgnoreCase` overload. The absence is load-bearing.
      3. File-header comment explains the design intent (parse-at-edge; H12c format preservation; item 3 axis).
      4. NO `[JsonConverter]` on the enum itself — the enum is a computed helper, not a serialization type.
         `ProvisioningRun.TenancyModel` stays `string` (Cosmos wire format preservation per constraint).
    </step>

    <step n="2" name="Add ProvisioningRun.ParsedTenancyModel computed helper (optional convenience)">
      Edit `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Models/ProvisioningRun.cs`:
      1. Add `public TenancyModel? TryGetParsedTenancyModel()` computed method returning `null` on failure —
         handlers that want to reject on failure use this + their own rejection code (matching H1's pattern).
      2. Do NOT add a `ParsedTenancyModel` property that throws on read — a property that can throw on
         serializer read would break Cosmos round-trips of legacy rows.
      3. Do NOT change the `TenancyModel` string property's shape or serialization.
      4. Update the XML doc on `TenancyModel` string property to reference the new enum + parser.
    </step>

    <step n="3" name="Migrate B1–B3 (single-literal comparisons)">
      Three files, each replacing `string.Equals(tenancyModel, "Model1Shared", ...)` with a parse-at-entry +
      typed switch. Kill callers before removing helpers so compile cascade stays local.
      1. **B1** `ArmDeploymentRunner.cs:232` (Bicep template blob key selection):
         - At the method entry that receives `tenancyModel` string, add
           `if (!TenancyModelParser.TryParse(tenancyModel, out var model)) throw new ArgumentException(...)`
           (or return a typed failure per the surrounding method contract — check whether the caller expects an
           exception or a Result-shape).
         - Replace the `string.Equals` branch with `model switch { TenancyModel.Model1Shared => ..., TenancyModel.Model2Dedicated => ... }` (exhaustive; no `_ =>` arm — compile-time C# 12 exhaustiveness).
      2. **B2** `FileBicepTemplateInspector.cs:110` — same pattern.
      3. **B3** `H2bAiSearchIndexHandler.cs:295` — same pattern.
      All three preserve their existing return-value semantics; only the branch mechanism changes.
    </step>

    <step n="4" name="Migrate B4/B5 + close P-2 defect (H1 CustomerOwnedTenancyValues)">
      Edit `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SubscriptionReadiness/H1SubscriptionReadinessHandler.cs`:
      1. Retire the two model literals from the sets:
         `CustomerOwnedTenancyValues = { "CustomerOwned" }` (was `{ "CustomerOwned", "Model2Dedicated" }`)
         `SpaarkeOwnedTenancyValues = { "SpaarkeOwned" }` (was `{ "SpaarkeOwned", "Model1Shared" }`)
      2. Update the logic that classifies tenancy → Lighthouse-required to use the enum:
         - Parse tenancyModel via `TenancyModelParser.TryParse` (H1's existing `InvalidTenancyModel` rejection
           code handles TryParse failure — the pattern is already present, just refactor to typed).
         - Map enum → ownership: `TenancyModel.Model1Shared` → SpaarkeOwned (no Lighthouse), `TenancyModel.Model2Dedicated`
           → CustomerOwned (Lighthouse required). This is the D-12 axis mapping documented in inventory §3.
         - The `CustomerOwnedTenancyValues` / `SpaarkeOwnedTenancyValues` sets remain — they're now used ONLY
           for the ownership-vocabulary classification (a caller passing "CustomerOwned" / "SpaarkeOwned"
           directly). Verify no downstream consumer relies on the retired model-literal membership; if any,
           escalate per trigger 6.
      3. Update `SubscriptionReadinessRejectionCodes.cs:57-59` XML doc to reference the enum (was
         `<c>SpaarkeOwned</c> / <c>Model1Shared</c> /` — retire the model literal, keep the ownership words).
      4. **This closes P-2**: H1 no longer demands Lighthouse for Spaarke-owned subscriptions holding a
         `Model2Dedicated` tenancy that D-12 has re-assigned to Spaarke's tenant. Post-Item-2, a
         Spaarke-hosted Model 2 profile classifies as SpaarkeOwned via the enum → no Lighthouse.
    </step>

    <step n="5" name="Migrate B6/B7 (AiSearchTenantFilterInvariantProbe)">
      Edit `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/AiSearchTenantFilterInvariantProbe.cs`:
      1. Delete the file-private constants `Model1TenancyModel` (L142) + `Model2TenancyModel` (L145) — these
         are a local tidy that the enum obsoletes.
      2. Replace L250 + L301 string comparisons with typed enum switch. Parse at the probe's own entry point;
         reject with a probe-specific error (existing probe result shape).
      3. Update comments at L72/L76 mentioning the literals to reference the enum type.
    </step>

    <step n="6" name="Migrate B8 (ArmCostEnvelopeChecker) + retire D4 + delete Model1SharedFloorEnvelopeUsd option">
      Edit `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/ArmCostEnvelopeChecker.cs`:
      1. Rewrite `SelectExpectedEnvelope(string tenancyModel)`:
         - Rename param to `TenancyModel tenancyModel` (accept enum, not string). Callers TryParse at their
           entry — this checker is called with an already-validated typed value.
